# Marketing-site pageviews for rivethub.io (PostHog). The project API key is
# public by design — it is baked into dist/posthog-config.js — but do not
# commit a live value. Leave unset to keep analytics off (local preview,
# CI without secrets).
#
# One PostHog project can be reused for rivetos.dev and rivethub.io; the
# hostname on each $pageview distinguishes the sites. Use a different key
# when building each site only if you want separate projects.
#
# GitHub: repository secrets PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY and optional
# PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST. pipeline.yml injects them into the CI Build job.
# Production deploys that publish dist/ must run this build with the same
# variables (the script also loads apps/rivethub-site/.env if present).

PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=
PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# House Next.js names are accepted as fallbacks if those secrets already exist:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=
